 75	  // the target GPU memory space, rebind its deallocation stream to this task's stream so that
 76	  // when the task later frees the data the free lands on the active stream's free list rather
 77	  // than on the stream the data was produced on. We use try_to_mutable() so we never block --
 78	  // if another reader holds the batch (e.g. a probe task on another GPU sharing a build batch)
 79	  // or it is otherwise busy, we simply skip the rebind; correctness is unaffected. Gating on a
 80	  // space match guarantees the stream and the data live on the same device (important for
 81	  // multi-GPU). The mismatch case below converts via `stream`, which already allocates the new
 82	  // table on it, so no rebind is needed there.
